Licensing and copyright notices for charr
==========================================

Package license
---------------

Charr's original code and documentation are copyright (c) 2026 Travers Ching.
Material derived from stringr is copyright (c) 2023 stringr authors. These
parts of the package are distributed under the MIT License.

`DESCRIPTION` declares `MIT + file LICENSE`. The top-level `LICENSE` is the
DCF-format completion of R's standard MIT template. It records Travers Ching
as the copyright holder for charr's original MIT-licensed work. The complete
MIT terms are reproduced below. Stringr's upstream notice is preserved in the
same license text and in the stringr section below.

The MIT package license does not replace the licenses and notices for the
included components described below.

